Z||000001||Borgio||12-02-2001||10:24 PM||||There are really only two different engines stock, the 140hp 2.8L V6 and the, i think, 90hp, 2.5L 4cyl. So, all the ones with the same engine are really about the same speed. Tranny's do make a difference. From personal experience, I would go with a manual. You can get a 6 for under $2k. Yes, you can even put an V8 in it. Really all stock fieros are very similar and if you're gonna drop an 8 in it, it won't matter all that much which one you get, especially if you do a lambo kit, which a good one would be expensive, btw. Lots of people who do kits just get the cheapest one they can get with a good frame, low miles is better too. Hope this helps. Correct me where I'm wrong people.||||reg||1
